{"revision":"0cbe25edd1687d3b926b498c10810c2759cadcf674b7c27691a0dc5a75a9f59c","generatedAt":"2026-09-03T08:51:50.583Z","app":{"id":"org.gnome.Calculator","slug":"calculator","name":"Calculator","summary":"Perform arithmetic, scientific or financial calculations","description":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Calculator is an application that solves mathematical equations. Though it at first appears to be a simple calculator with only basic arithmetic operations, you can switch into Advanced, Financial, or Programming mode to find a surprising set of capabilities."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The Advanced calculator supports many operations, including: logarithms, factorials, trigonometric and hyperbolic functions, modulus division, complex numbers, random number generation and prime factorization."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Financial mode supports several computations, including periodic interest rate, present and future value, double declining and straight line depreciation, and many others."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Programming mode supports calculations using common bases (binary, octal, decimal, and hexadecimal), bitwise operations, two’s complement, character to character code conversion, and more."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Conversion mode supports conversions between common units, currencies and number bases."}]}],"projectLicense":"GPL-3.0-or-later","developer":{"name":"The GNOME Project"},"homepage":"https://apps.gnome.org/Calculator","repository":"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-calculator","links":{"bugtracker":"https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-calculator/issues","help":"https://help.gnome.org/users/gnome-calculator/stable/","donation":"https://www.gnome.org/donate/","translate":"https://l10n.gnome.org/module/gnome-calculator/"},"contentRating":{"label":"Early Childhood","minimumAge":3},"keywords":[